H("jobscheduler-hld", "Design a distributed job scheduler (cron at scale)", "Advanced",
  ["Amazon", "Google", "Microsoft", "Uber", "Airbnb"],
  "Reliable timing, exactly-once execution, scaling workers, retries.",
  ["Schedule one-off and recurring (cron) jobs", "Run jobs on a worker fleet", "Retries, timeouts, job history and status"],
  ["Millions of jobs/day", "A job runs once per schedule (no duplicates, no misses)", "Fire within seconds of scheduled time"],
  "- 10M executions/day ≈ 120/s, bursts at round hours (00:00) of 100k+.",
  "`POST /jobs {schedule: cron|runAt, payload, retryPolicy, timeout}` · `GET /jobs/{id}/runs` · `DELETE /jobs/{id}`",
  "`jobs(id, schedule, next_run_at, ...)` partitioned by `next_run_at` bucket; `runs(job_id, scheduled_for, status, attempt, worker, lease_until)` with unique `(job_id, scheduled_for)`.",
  {"rows": [["Clients"], ["Job API"], ["db:Jobs DB (partitioned by time)"], ["Scheduler shards (poll due jobs)"], ["q:Execution queue"], ["Workers"], ["db:Run history"]],
   "edges": [["Clients", "Job API"], ["Job API", "Jobs DB (partitioned by time)"], ["Scheduler shards (poll due jobs)", "Jobs DB (partitioned by time)", "due in next 30s"], ["Scheduler shards (poll due jobs)", "Execution queue"], ["Execution queue", "Workers"], ["Workers", "Run history", "status/lease"]]},
  ["Scheduler shards each own a range of partitions (via leader election/lease); every few seconds they fetch jobs due soon, insert a `run` row (unique per job+time → no duplicates), enqueue it, and compute `next_run_at`.",
   "Workers take runs, heartbeat a lease, execute (idempotently), record success; expired leases are retried."],
  ["Unique constraint for exactly-once scheduling; idempotent jobs for at-least-once execution.", "Time-bucketed partitions avoid scanning everything.", "Jitter for jobs at popular times.", "Priorities and per-tenant quotas.", "Workflow DAGs (Airflow/Temporal) as an extension."]),

